# Regex literal invalid pattern rejected

Verifies a pattern the regex engine cannot compile is rejected at compile
time: the unclosed character class surfaces the engine error with its source
span instead of producing a value.

>>> source
bad: regex = /[unclosed/
print(bad)

<<< stdout

<<< stderr
eck: invalid literal `/[unclosed/` for type `regex`: regex parse error:
    [unclosed
    ^
error: unclosed character class at Span { start: 13, end: 24 }

<<< exit
1
